<Page title="Editorial Policy" description="StateMaps' editorial standards: independence, sourcing, corrections and how we use AI tools." path="/editorial-policy/" updated="November 8, 2026">
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>Our rankings are decided by our editors using the criteria in <a href="/how-we-review/">How we review</a>. Developers can't pay for inclusion, rank, or favorable wording, and they don't see articles before publication.</p>
  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <p>Factual claims about features, pricing, encryption and data handling are checked against primary sources: the developer's website and documentation, app store listings, privacy policies, and published audits or source code. Where we couldn't confirm a claim, we say so or leave it out.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If we get something wrong, we fix it and update the page date. Send corrections through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Use of AI tools</h2>
  <p>We use AI tools to help with research and drafting. Every published page is reviewed and fact-checked by our team against primary sources before it goes live, and we are responsible for everything we publish.</p>
  <h2>Safety</h2>
  <p>We write about privacy tools for legitimate personal privacy. We don't publish guides for monitoring other people without their knowledge or for bypassing someone else's device security.</p>
</Page>
